                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a0bd013-7f41-3584-9282-ca92b743c232",
                        "entry_id": "490ef3a6-e0b7-32b4-992c-1ddd78fe597f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of electric vehicle (a type of road vehicle)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "820fb4ad-2e2a-4fe5-ab1b-23a11edf9a2a",
                                "sense_id": "2a0bd013-7f41-3584-9282-ca92b743c232",
                                "text": "But compared with gasoline or diesel-powered cars and trucks, E.V.s also require special or seriously modified components, and out-of-the-ordinary mechanical and physical attention (or inattention, as we’ll see below)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a65b71ca-206f-40f0-a23f-8159a2787a18",
                                "sense_id": "2a0bd013-7f41-3584-9282-ca92b743c232",
                                "text": "Despite progress towards a 2045 zero-emission goal, the high price of EVs has created a headache for governments[.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae1a4296-6fc5-4bf2-851b-680f41c96bdb",
                                "sense_id": "2a0bd013-7f41-3584-9282-ca92b743c232",
                                "text": "The automakers are pleased with the slower ramp-up. \"Moderating the pace of EV adoption in 2027, 2028, 2029, and 2030 was the right call because it prioritizes more reasonable electrification targets in the next few (very critical) years of the EV transition."
                            }
                        ]
